    "result_text": "Corrections are in, and the Playwright test passes on its first run (`bin/e2e`: 1 passed).\n\n**What a correction does now**\n- A claim with a negative amount is only accepted if the claim form's new \"corrects\" field gives the number of a SETTLED claim of the same person. Otherwise it is refused: the form shows `claim-form-error` and nothing is saved or written to the audit file.\n- The screen checks this before sending, and the server checks it again (`CheckClaimCorrects`, a new step in both the add-claim and edit-claim endpoints), so a request that skips the screen is refused too.\n- A correction's due is its amount times the rate, with no floor and no late charge. That applies when it is settled, when its due is shown live, and when a period is closed.\n- Each claim row shows the number a correction corrects (`claim-corrects`, empty for other claims). The audit lines are unchanged.\n\n**Other changes**\n- The stored data has a new nullable `claim.corrects` column (migration `V20__claim_corrects.sql`).\n- **Front-end sign bug fixed:** the front end's money maths mishandled negative values. For example, `-0.50` was read as +0.50, and a negative total didn't display correctly. Both are fixed, because otherwise the totals would have come out wrong once corrections existed.\n\n**Choices the request didn't settle**\n- **Positive amounts can't name a claim:** filling in \"corrects\" on a claim of 0.00 or more is refused rather than ignored.\n- **Corrections can be corrected:** a correction may name any settled claim, including another settled correction. The test relies on this (it corrects claim 2, which is itself a correction).\n- **Quick-add stays non-negative**, since it has no \"corrects\" field.\n- **Corrections can still show as overdue:** I left the overdue logic as it was, so only the late charge is dropped for them.",
